      "before": "---\ntitle: \"Artifacts & provenance\"\ndescription: \"Every analysis output is durable, downloadable, and fully traceable to its origin.\"\nowner: \"docs\"\n---\n\nEvery completed turn persists its outputs: plots as PNG, tables as CSV,\nscalars as JSON, plus an operation record capturing the exact\n`{operation_id, params}` that ran. An artifact cannot exist without complete\nprovenance — the invariant is enforced in the storage schema itself.\n\n## What provenance answers\n\nWhich source file (id and content hash), which operation, which parameters,\nwhich package versions were installed at the moment of computation, when it\nran, and how long it took. Versions are captured from the kernel response\nthat produced the numbers — never looked up after the fact.\n\n## Lineage\n\nWhen a turn runs on a previous result table, the new artifacts record the\nparent artifact id. The artifact page shows the chain.\n\n## Retention\n\n{/* concord:fact key=retention.artifact.days */}\nArtifacts are retained for 30 days after creation; the expiry date is shown\non the artifact page.\n",
